WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.122 --> 00:00:01.362
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:01.362 --> 00:00:04.398
My name is Evan Carmichael,
my one word is believe.

00:00:04.398 --> 00:00:06.311
And I believe that
entrepreneurs are going to

00:00:06.311 --> 00:00:09.539
solve all of the world's major problems.

00:00:09.539 --> 00:00:11.727
So to help you on your
journey today's message

00:00:11.727 --> 00:00:14.933
is prepare yourself for success.

00:00:14.933 --> 00:00:16.525
Over to you Dr. Sunday Adelaja.

00:00:16.525 --> 00:00:19.162
(rooster)

00:00:19.162 --> 00:00:21.162
(music)

00:00:28.748 --> 00:00:31.285
- Success is possible,
success is a reality.

00:00:31.285 --> 00:00:35.060
But the fact is that only
people who are well prepared

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:38.213
get the blessings of success in life.

00:00:38.213 --> 00:00:40.052
You know, it's like life is not fair

00:00:40.052 --> 00:00:43.290
it is a (mumbles) in some cases.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.179
If you look at it just from the surface.

00:00:45.179 --> 00:00:47.065
And you think that, you see some people

00:00:47.065 --> 00:00:49.958
who are making it, some people
who are doing a good job.

00:00:49.958 --> 00:00:51.858
And some people who are
really making it in life.

00:00:51.858 --> 00:00:53.259
And you think, what makes these people

00:00:53.259 --> 00:00:54.543
better than the other people?

00:00:54.543 --> 00:00:57.111
And it's like there's not
really any much difference.

00:00:57.111 --> 00:00:59.124
But really, there is a difference.

00:00:59.124 --> 00:01:00.941
If you see anybody that
is truly making it,

00:01:00.941 --> 00:01:02.467
that is doing a good job,

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:05.488
it is only because it's
done something right.

00:01:05.488 --> 00:01:09.334
And the major condition,
or the major thing

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:10.853
a person like that has done right,

00:01:10.853 --> 00:01:13.521
is that they have gotten
themselves prepared

00:01:13.521 --> 00:01:15.738
for this success that they now enjoy.

00:01:15.738 --> 00:01:16.867
Only opportunities come

00:01:16.867 --> 00:01:18.998
only to people who are prepared for them.

00:01:18.998 --> 00:01:20.704
If you are not prepared for opportunities,

00:01:20.704 --> 00:01:21.786
you will never see them,

00:01:21.786 --> 00:01:23.597
you will think that there are
no opportunities around you.

00:01:23.597 --> 00:01:26.015
People complain about the
countries they live in,

00:01:26.015 --> 00:01:27.831
people complain about their leaders,

00:01:27.831 --> 00:01:29.531
people complain about their environment,

00:01:29.531 --> 00:01:32.724
and they all complain that
there are no opportunities

00:01:32.724 --> 00:01:34.596
in their countries, or in their cities,

00:01:34.596 --> 00:01:35.633
or from their leaders.

00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:38.396
But really, even in those countries,

00:01:38.396 --> 00:01:41.431
even in those cities,
there are people who are

00:01:41.431 --> 00:01:43.964
having opportunities, who are, you know,

00:01:43.964 --> 00:01:47.787
being entrusted by life, by
great positions of opportunities

00:01:47.787 --> 00:01:51.196
because they are prepared for them.

00:01:51.196 --> 00:01:54.015
- So if you want to be successful,
you have to do the work

00:01:54.015 --> 00:01:56.554
to be prepared for when it comes to you.

00:01:56.554 --> 00:01:59.217
Success doesn't just land on your lap,

00:01:59.217 --> 00:02:01.642
opportunities don't just
open themselves up to you,

00:02:01.642 --> 00:02:03.097
you have to do the work.

00:02:03.097 --> 00:02:05.458
It doesn't come by just
sitting on the couch

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.608
and dreaming and thinking and hoping that

00:02:07.608 --> 00:02:09.217
something's going to happen to you.

00:02:09.217 --> 00:02:11.810
It happens because you are
out, and you are preparing

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:14.463
and you are doing the work.

00:02:14.463 --> 00:02:16.258
So as an example, I look at Lily,

00:02:16.258 --> 00:02:18.503
who was one of my salsa
instructors, still is,

00:02:18.503 --> 00:02:22.281
and I offered her a full time
opportunity to quit her job

00:02:22.281 --> 00:02:24.028
and start her own business

00:02:24.028 --> 00:02:26.895
as a new potential speaker with me.

00:02:26.895 --> 00:02:28.415
And I paid her to leave her job

00:02:28.415 --> 00:02:30.212
so she can start this opportunity.

00:02:30.212 --> 00:02:32.447
So she's getting paid to leave her job,

00:02:32.447 --> 00:02:34.824
she's getting mentoring from
me to launch her own business

00:02:34.824 --> 00:02:37.030
and a lot of people would think,

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:39.139
well how do I get that opportunity?

00:02:39.139 --> 00:02:40.712
How do I get that chance to do it?

00:02:40.712 --> 00:02:42.383
You're so lucky that you get this thing

00:02:42.383 --> 00:02:43.778
that nobody else gets.

00:02:43.778 --> 00:02:46.527
But she did the work to prepare for it.

00:02:46.527 --> 00:02:49.139
She was putting in hustle
and energy and heart

00:02:49.139 --> 00:02:51.261
and from one of the first
times that I met her,

00:02:51.261 --> 00:02:52.273
and had our conversation,

00:02:52.273 --> 00:02:53.459
I said, I want to do something with you,

00:02:53.459 --> 00:02:54.478
we're going to figure out a way,

00:02:54.478 --> 00:02:57.525
some kind of business to happen together.

00:02:57.525 --> 00:02:58.577
And she might have thought I was crazy

00:02:58.577 --> 00:03:00.590
the first time that we
had that conversation.

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:03.861
- During the meeting, he told
me that he really liked me

00:03:03.861 --> 00:03:06.862
and he wanted to start some
sort of business with me.

00:03:06.862 --> 00:03:09.563
So my first thought was, wow!

00:03:09.563 --> 00:03:10.730
He is so nice.

00:03:12.038 --> 00:03:15.607
And what an amazing
confidence booster for me.

00:03:15.607 --> 00:03:18.336
- But she worked at it and she prepared

00:03:18.336 --> 00:03:21.658
and she put in hours
and effort consistently

00:03:21.658 --> 00:03:22.660
and that's the difference.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.016
If you look at anybody
who's had major success,

00:03:25.016 --> 00:03:26.461
look at anybody who you look up to,

00:03:26.461 --> 00:03:28.592
as an entrepreneur, as an athlete,

00:03:28.592 --> 00:03:30.685
as a singer, whatever you aspire to do,

00:03:30.685 --> 00:03:33.665
there is always a ton of hard work

00:03:33.665 --> 00:03:35.387
that goes alongside it.

00:03:35.387 --> 00:03:37.347
You will not get the success you're after

00:03:37.347 --> 00:03:39.041
by just sitting on the couch.

00:03:39.041 --> 00:03:40.899
And when an opportunity does come to you,

00:03:40.899 --> 00:03:43.032
you have to say yes to it.

00:03:43.032 --> 00:03:45.375
Before I offered Lily this position,

00:03:45.375 --> 00:03:47.564
I actually offered a different position

00:03:47.564 --> 00:03:48.808
to somebody else.

00:03:48.808 --> 00:03:51.829
To a guy who I was going to
start a marketing agency with.

00:03:51.829 --> 00:03:55.100
And he said no, he said he
wasn't ready to quit his job.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:56.905
And he didn't jump on that opportunity.

00:03:56.905 --> 00:03:59.110
And so I had the space
to offer it to Lily.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:03.174
If he said yes, to that
opportunity three months sooner,

00:04:03.174 --> 00:04:04.844
I wouldn't have been
able to give it to Lily

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:06.862
because my time would have been taken up.

00:04:06.862 --> 00:04:09.354
But he said no, he's down on his copa path

00:04:09.354 --> 00:04:10.799
and Lily said yes.

00:04:10.799 --> 00:04:12.460
So when those opportunities come,

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:13.747
and when they're scary,

00:04:13.747 --> 00:04:15.384
and when you're not sure
how it's going to work out,

00:04:15.384 --> 00:04:17.841
do you seize it or not?

00:04:17.841 --> 00:04:20.035
Or do you live the rest
of your life in regret

00:04:20.035 --> 00:04:22.162
wondering, what might have happened?

00:04:22.162 --> 00:04:24.082
So the question of the
day today is I'm curious,

00:04:24.082 --> 00:04:27.048
what is the thing that
you are doing consistently

00:04:27.048 --> 00:04:29.143
to prepare yourself for success?

00:04:29.143 --> 00:04:31.932
How much are you working on
your dream, on your goal,

00:04:31.932 --> 00:04:35.364
every single day to make
sure that it happens?

00:04:35.364 --> 00:04:36.574
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:04:36.574 --> 00:04:37.945
I'm super curious to find out.

00:04:37.945 --> 00:04:40.041
I also want to give a quick
shoutout to John Jenkins.

00:04:40.041 --> 00:04:42.320
John, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:45.118
"Your One Word" and making that
Youtube video about it man,

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:48.310
I really appreciate it and
I thank you for the support,

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:50.047
I'm glad you enjoyed the read.

00:04:50.047 --> 00:04:52.693
So thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you,

00:04:52.693 --> 00:04:54.786
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:04:54.786 --> 00:04:57.991
and whatever your one word is, much love

00:04:57.991 --> 00:04:59.402
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:04:59.402 --> 00:05:01.935
for another shot of espresso.

00:05:01.935 --> 00:05:03.935
(music)

00:05:10.925 --> 00:05:12.895
- I wake up about 4:30 and 5:00

00:05:12.895 --> 00:05:16.380
and between 5 and 5:15
I am working on email,

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.452
catching up on news, looking at the blogs,

00:05:18.452 --> 00:05:20.193
looking at the different opinions.

00:05:20.193 --> 00:05:21.629
Because people just don't sleep,

00:05:21.629 --> 00:05:24.212
I mean they are working 24/7,
somewhere around the world

00:05:24.212 --> 00:05:25.431
people are awake and working.

00:05:25.431 --> 00:05:27.469
So have this constantly being bombarded

00:05:27.469 --> 00:05:31.663
with requests, information,
or just sometimes news.

00:05:31.663 --> 00:05:33.720
And so in the morning I wake up and I

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.112
you know, take care of my mind.

00:05:36.112 --> 00:05:38.112
(music)

00:05:41.527 --> 00:05:43.021
And then after that I work out

00:05:43.021 --> 00:05:45.854
and that's taking care of my body.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.706
And then I do meditate before I go to work

00:05:49.706 --> 00:05:52.058
so that takes care of my soul.

00:05:52.058 --> 00:05:53.662
In a business, it's like a war.

00:05:53.662 --> 00:05:56.412
You have to be completely prepared.

00:05:56.412 --> 00:05:58.401
And unless you have mind, body, and soul

00:05:58.401 --> 00:06:01.633
really all ready for it, you
just can't fight that battle.

00:06:01.633 --> 00:06:03.280
- How often do you find
when you get on set,

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:06.227
people are like, do the Samuel,
do the Sam Jackson thing?

00:06:06.227 --> 00:06:09.309
Do the Samuel Jackson thing
that we know and love?

00:06:09.309 --> 00:06:10.158
- Not often.

00:06:10.158 --> 00:06:10.991
- [Male Interviewer] No.

00:06:10.991 --> 00:06:12.092
- I don't know what that is.

00:06:12.092 --> 00:06:13.063
(laughing)

00:06:13.063 --> 00:06:13.896
I mean,

00:06:15.344 --> 00:06:17.237
unless you say motherfucker
like eight times.

00:06:17.237 --> 00:06:19.487
(laughing)

00:06:20.321 --> 00:06:22.307
You know, well crafted play.

00:06:22.307 --> 00:06:23.389
(cheering)

00:06:23.389 --> 00:06:24.976
But umm..

00:06:24.976 --> 00:06:27.626
Yeah I don't, I don't
really know what that is

00:06:27.626 --> 00:06:31.255
or to me, the Sam Jackson thing is

00:06:31.255 --> 00:06:35.848
I've read the script, you know,
I don't know how many times

00:06:35.848 --> 00:06:38.792
and I've broken my character down

00:06:38.792 --> 00:06:40.436
the way I've learned to
break a character down

00:06:40.436 --> 00:06:42.370
in the theater.

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:44.226
If there's source material, like for

00:06:44.226 --> 00:06:45.526
George Washington Williams,

00:06:45.526 --> 00:06:47.407
I'll go through the source
material and deal with that,

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:49.848
but if not, then, okay, it's up to me

00:06:49.848 --> 00:06:51.202
to figure out who this guy is.

00:06:51.202 --> 00:06:53.990
I can figure out when he was
born, who his parents were,

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:55.919
what his educational background is.

00:06:55.919 --> 00:06:58.002
Military, if he has that.

00:06:58.887 --> 00:07:01.980
What kind of life experiences he's had,

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:03.667
how he feels about
this, that or the other.

00:07:03.667 --> 00:07:06.470
Even down to sometimes what
kind of food he eats, you know.

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:08.817
Just because there are
eatin scenes in the movie

00:07:08.817 --> 00:07:11.275
and I want to figure out
what I want to eat, you know

00:07:11.275 --> 00:07:13.262
when I'm in that particular scene.

00:07:13.262 --> 00:07:14.983
And then, from scene to scene,

00:07:14.983 --> 00:07:17.162
what my relationship is
with those characters,

00:07:17.162 --> 00:07:19.125
or what I'm trying to
accomplish in this scene

00:07:19.125 --> 00:07:21.077
that leads to the next scene,
that leads to the next scene

00:07:21.077 --> 00:07:22.533
that leads to the next scene.

00:07:22.533 --> 00:07:26.473
So, what happens is, the
Sam Jackson thing, for me

00:07:26.473 --> 00:07:29.715
according to my agents and managers is

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:32.798
I'm so prepared, when I show up, that

00:07:34.591 --> 00:07:37.170
I expect everybody else
to be as prepared as I am.

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:41.012
So when the director does not
have a shot list for that day,

00:07:41.012 --> 00:07:44.017
or directors floundering
and trying to figure out

00:07:44.017 --> 00:07:47.392
what he's doing, he can
ask me and I can tell him.

00:07:47.392 --> 00:07:51.485
You know, because one of the
funny things about movies is

00:07:51.485 --> 00:07:54.152
the directors usually the
person on the film set

00:07:54.152 --> 00:07:55.978
that's got the least amount of experience

00:07:55.978 --> 00:07:57.561
of everybody there.

00:07:59.077 --> 00:08:00.372
(laughing)

00:08:00.372 --> 00:08:03.168
- A director makes one
movie every four years,

00:08:03.168 --> 00:08:04.657
every two years...

00:08:04.657 --> 00:08:06.505
- But director's career is what?

00:08:06.505 --> 00:08:08.765
A good director's career is 15 movies.

00:08:08.765 --> 00:08:10.877
You know, everybody
there has done 15 movies

00:08:10.877 --> 00:08:12.442
the last two years.

00:08:12.442 --> 00:08:15.142
You know, so, we all know, you know

00:08:15.142 --> 00:08:16.825
why the fuck he using that, that
ain't going to be in the movie

00:08:16.825 --> 00:08:19.345
(laughing)

00:08:19.345 --> 00:08:21.317
It's like, you don't
really need that shot.

00:08:21.317 --> 00:08:22.515
(coughing)

00:08:22.515 --> 00:08:24.765
(laughing)

00:08:27.624 --> 00:08:29.369
So, there's that shit goin.

00:08:29.369 --> 00:08:30.845
Where did I digress from?

00:08:30.845 --> 00:08:32.335
- No that was amazing (mumbles)

00:08:32.335 --> 00:08:34.386
I don't care that we digressed.

00:08:34.386 --> 00:08:35.968
- I show up prepared.

00:08:35.968 --> 00:08:38.602
So that's the Sam Jackson thing.

00:08:38.602 --> 00:08:41.825
When you hire me, you hire an
actor who going to show up,

00:08:41.825 --> 00:08:44.312
who going to know his lines,
who going to hit his marks

00:08:44.312 --> 00:08:46.677
and do his best to make the other actors

00:08:46.677 --> 00:08:48.698
around him better.

00:08:48.698 --> 00:08:49.531
- [Interviewer] Absolutely.

00:08:49.531 --> 00:08:51.536
- I'm not going to call shots for you,

00:08:51.536 --> 00:08:56.085
and I don't expect you to
give me a line reading.

00:08:56.085 --> 00:08:58.402
And if you do, you hired
the wrong motherfucker.

00:08:58.402 --> 00:08:59.999
(laughing)

00:08:59.999 --> 00:09:01.703
- With doubt, which
might be the first time

00:09:01.703 --> 00:09:04.267
that people in film, necessarily really

00:09:04.267 --> 00:09:05.481
appreciated what you were doing.

00:09:05.481 --> 00:09:07.608
(clapping)

00:09:07.608 --> 00:09:12.553
Your preparation for that
was astronomical, amazing

00:09:12.553 --> 00:09:16.274
and, so the last, as the
last pre-Help question,

00:09:16.274 --> 00:09:19.047
if I can just ask you, just
to show the kind of work

00:09:19.047 --> 00:09:20.523
that you're willing to do, for even,

00:09:20.523 --> 00:09:22.553
I think it was eight
minutes of screen time?

00:09:22.553 --> 00:09:25.514
Which was deservedly rewarded
with an Oscar nomination

00:09:25.514 --> 00:09:27.800
but I mean, that is
not a ton to work with,

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:29.178
and yet, you made the most of it.

00:09:29.178 --> 00:09:33.461
How did you, what did you
do to prepare for that one?

00:09:33.461 --> 00:09:36.560
- Well, it's based on a
play, so I read the play

00:09:36.560 --> 00:09:37.969
and after I read the play I said,

00:09:37.969 --> 00:09:39.727
I don't even understand this woman.

00:09:39.727 --> 00:09:41.770
I don't know why this
got all this attention.

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:43.503
This woman wants to sacrifice her son,

00:09:43.503 --> 00:09:44.870
and duh duh duh duh dah.

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:48.539
And I had all the kind of
responses that you would have

00:09:48.539 --> 00:09:50.544
with character that you didn't understand.

00:09:50.544 --> 00:09:54.711
But, it's being an actor, you
have to do investigative work.

00:09:56.786 --> 00:10:00.990
You have to, you have to,
make sure that when people

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:05.131
are in the audience, they understand you.

00:10:05.131 --> 00:10:08.705
And they ultimately feel something.

00:10:08.705 --> 00:10:11.122
And so, I had to write a bio,

00:10:12.248 --> 00:10:15.318
which ended up being over 100 pages.

00:10:15.318 --> 00:10:17.919
I talked to people who had seen the play,

00:10:17.919 --> 00:10:19.751
cause I was doing a play at the same time

00:10:19.751 --> 00:10:21.241
and never saw the play.

00:10:21.241 --> 00:10:24.770
I read the script, probably,
I don't know how many times.

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:28.219
So I literally studied
the script for four months

00:10:28.219 --> 00:10:32.386
before I finally got it,
like I had the aha moment.

00:10:33.247 --> 00:10:37.777
And the aha moment, is,
we always want to feel

00:10:37.777 --> 00:10:39.944
that decisions are pretty.

00:10:41.271 --> 00:10:44.858
We always want to believe
that decisions are easy.

00:10:44.858 --> 00:10:48.745
And sometimes there are so fews choice.

00:10:48.745 --> 00:10:52.403
You know, and sometimes
a person's motivations

00:10:52.403 --> 00:10:54.070
are absolutely pure.

00:10:55.499 --> 00:10:59.666
But to the outside eye, they
look very dysfunctional.

00:11:00.768 --> 00:11:04.137
And I probably, you
know, had the aha moment

00:11:04.137 --> 00:11:06.505
two days before I even started filming

00:11:06.505 --> 00:11:08.420
and I was really waiting
for that aha moment

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:11.985
cause I said, I'm going to
be opposite Meryl Streep

00:11:11.985 --> 00:11:14.810
and she's going to tear me a new a-hole.

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:17.474
And I do not want to look bad.

00:11:17.474 --> 00:11:19.557
So I had that aha moment.

00:11:20.461 --> 00:11:23.628
But I did my, I did my work with that.

00:11:24.527 --> 00:11:27.618
I can't emphasize that enough, you know,

00:11:27.618 --> 00:11:31.383
because I never want
anyone to dismiss my talent

00:11:31.383 --> 00:11:33.551
listen, I may get up on this screen

00:11:33.551 --> 00:11:36.502
and there are times when I may stink

00:11:36.502 --> 00:11:39.901
because it's occupational
hazard to not always be good.

00:11:39.901 --> 00:11:44.068
But I never want anyone to
say that she's not an actress.

